    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** headlines our output with a score of 62.58, securing his spot in the OF4 slot despite a neutral matchup against Drohan. While the L-on-L disadvantage against Drohan (3.91 xERA) shaves 1% off his projection, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s elite base skill and prime placement in the 5-hole provide enough structural support to justify a strong start. **Andy Pages** also cracks the starting lineup at 50.60; while his 8-hole assignment limits his run-production ceiling, his ability to navigate the secondary starter metrics keeps him above our 40.0 floor, providing essential depth for today\u2019s rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Liam Hicks**, whose 38.17 score left him just shy of the 40.0 threshold. Despite a +11% boost from a favorable platoon advantage against Williams, the high-skill profile of the opposing pitcher (2.95 xERA) severely hampered his expected output, ultimately forcing us to hold him in reserve to maintain our daily game cap efficiency. **Brayan Rocchio** also fell short of the starting cut, as his 9-hole placement and a less-than-ideal matchup against Jax contributed to a stagnant score of 36.92. \n\nWe remain in a holding pattern regarding the rest of the roster, including **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg**, as we monitor daily lineup movements across the league. Note that **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, and **Jackson Merrill** is effectively off the table today due to an organizational off-day. With the scarceness of stolen bases in our current 5x5 build, we are prioritizing high-contact, high-sprint profiles like **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler** for future rotations, provided their matchups against sub-4.00 xERA arms improve. Maintain discipline with our game caps; we are strictly adhering to the 40.0 efficiency floor to maximize long-term Roto value.",
